## What this track proposes

The track draws the 31 card rows that list v7 adds to the Storytime Level 2 print list. Each
card needs a color picture and a line-art picture, so the track delivers 62 files at 1500 x 1500.
It reuses the approved Storytime Muse path, the frozen Sonnet judge kit, and the week delivery
form, and it adds no new kit. It also moves the T180 version 3 list fixture from
/tmp/opencode/wb-shadow into the repository. The spend cap is 1.60 USD, the delivery is model
evidence only, and Workbooks checks the cards after delivery.

## How the current system works, per this spec

The closed unit 1 track holds the Muse path: scripts/storytime-muse.mjs calls meta/muse-image
through OpenRouter and writes the print file to the spec outDir. scripts/storytime-muse-guards.mjs
reads every costs.tsv below out/storytime/l2/unit1/ and enforces 3 tries per id and kind, a
1.00 USD cap since 2026-11-04T07:54:00Z, and a 0.50 USD report point.
scripts/storytime-judge-batch.mjs builds judge batches for the A-48 specs at a 360 px long side for
a card. The A-48 delivery form is the StorytimeManifest object in src/storytime/book-pictures.ts,
with the MANIFEST.txt form of the week handoff. Two tests read the version 3 list from
/tmp/opencode/wb-shadow, and that path is not in git.

## Checks run

Zoom-out. The scope matches the owner order, with no speculative feature and no premature
optimization. The spec reuses the Muse path, the guard module, the judge kit, and the delivery
form, and it cites each of them by file and symbol. New logic sits in the card spec folder, the
guard module, and the card tests. The specification stays at the requirement level.

Zero-decision. The card count, the file names, the size, the aspect, the prompt sources, the try
limits, the cap, the report point, the delivery paths, the manifest form, and the Drive folder are
all named. The judge-batch card input shape stays open (F1), and the owner of the card start time
is unnamed (F2). The absent Workbooks checkout edge case is undefined (F3).

Fact checks. 227 list rows, 31 card rows, and the first 196 rows are non-card. All 13 reference
paths exist. The spec-file form matches docs/storytime/l2-unit1/a48/l2-w08-check-row-drum.json.
The gate controls in calibration-set.json carry expected fail. The guard constants and the
scanCostFiles scope match the spec, so cards/muse/ falls inside the restart scan as the risk
section states. longSideOf returns 360 for a card. SPEC_DIR and RESTART_START are fixed, and
parseArgs has no flag for a spec folder or a start time. The orchestrator confirmed the four input
SHA-256 values with sha256sum on 2026-11-06; the reviewer could not run sha256sum because the
shell tool is denied in this role.

Note. measure/anti-patterns.md does not exist in this repository, and no file of that name
