## Findings

- F1 [Blocker] plan.md Task 2: The plan says the judge batch reads the card specs and counts card
  tries from the card start time, but it names no input shape for that.
  scripts/storytime-judge-batch.mjs:36 fixes SPEC_DIR to the A-48 folder, line 43 fixes
  RESTART_START, and parseArgs (lines 183-198) has no flag for a spec folder or a start time.
  Rationale: The implementer must choose between a new flag, an environment variable, or an added
  default folder. That is an API and CLI shape choice, so Red and Green can pick differently.
- F2 [Major] spec.md Tries and spend: The spec says the card run start time is a constant that
  Task 2 sets, but it names no single owner for the value. Plan Task 2 also says the judge batch
  counts card tries from the card start time. Rationale: A second copy of the constant in
  scripts/storytime-judge-batch.mjs (RESTART_START, line 43) can drift from the guard value, and
  the try count then reads the wrong rows. Name one exported constant and the module that imports
  it.
- F3 [Major] spec.md FR-3 and plan.md Task 3: The card spec test reads
  /home/daniebo/Desktop/Workbooks/content/storytime/l2/print/pictures.json, and the plan defines a
  SHA mismatch as a hard failure. The plan does not define the case where the Workbooks checkout
  is absent. Rationale: No test in tests/ reads that absolute path today, so the new test fails a
  full suite run on every checkout without Workbooks. Define the absent-file edge case.
- F4 [Nit] plan.md Task markers: Every work task uses [b], and the doctor counts only [ ], [~],
  and [x]. Rationale: A role that reads the marker list sees no open work task for this track.

## Recommendations

1. Name the judge-batch card input in plan.md Task 2: the flag or config that points at
   docs/storytime/l2-unit1/cards, and the flag or config that sets the card start time.
2. Name one owner for the card start time constant in spec.md Tries and spend, and name the
   module that imports it.
3. Define the absent Workbooks checkout case in plan.md Task 3. A missing file and a SHA mismatch
   need not take the same path.
4. Do not change the [b] markers unless another role reads them as a task list.

